HW-TSO · chain-csum · ack-merge tout 512 us&#10;• identity provisioning once/boot: devmem 0x9000_0600 group (aecp_csr_setup.sh, caps 0x8588)&#10;• PHC /dev/ptpN + SO_TIMESTAMPING expose the fabric clock; the product-default gPTP owner remains in fabric" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=5;spacingRight=5;" vertex="1" parent="c_drv"><mxGeometry x="15" y="35" width="1490" height="280" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="ptpd" value="gPTP exact-one owner: product-default KL_gptp_shadow/gptp-processor owns BMCA, servo and pdelay and publishes GM/parent/PHC state;&#10;only the explicit software-owner option-off comparison starts linuxptp + phc2sys/gptp2csr — never concurrently" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=5;spacingRight=5;" vertex="1" parent="c_drv"><mxGeometry x="15" y="335" width="1490" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="pw" value="media rev 3 (2026-08-13): softcore only fills a DMA PCM ring (ms cadence); fabric does SRP (MSRP/MVRP + admission),&#10;AAF framer (PTP presentation time) and the ACMP bind record - all three from the protocol processor. NO AECP anywhere." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=5;spacingRight=5;" vertex="1" parent="c_drv"><mxGeometry x="15" y="465" width="1490" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="qspihdr" value="QSPI flash N25Q128 16 MB (off-chip, flashboot slots):" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#faf6fc;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=9;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=5;spacingRight=5;" vertex="1" parent="c_drv"><mxGeometry x="15" y="595" width="1490" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="r_qspi0" value="FLASHED v1: kernel@0 · opensbi@0x88_0000 · dtb@0x90_0000 · rootfs@0x94_0000 — S